{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1777645962842,"sessionID":"ses_21c0b4c31ffer7LMtrt0SdVftq","part":{"id":"prt_de3f4bda0001ciJ81CFThRUhwd","messageID":"msg_de3f4b46a001Aq8oRDnDZ3Jmoi","sessionID":"ses_21c0b4c31ffer7LMtrt0SdVftq","type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_c4f39d91218c47efbc823a49","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__7855_7794_1777645357.txt"},"output":"<path>/home/jinxu/opencode-spawn-pilot/outputs/opencode_spawn_pilot/comparison_v12_single/.prompt_musique_2hop__7855_7794_1777645357.txt</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: You are a research agent answering multi-hop questions by searching through documents.\n2: \n3: Your task: Read the provided documents, find the information needed to answer the question, and output your answer.\n4: \n5: RULES:\n6: - Use the read and grep tools to search through documents\n7: - Base your answer ONLY on information found in the documents\n8: - Do not guess or use your own knowledge\n9: \n10: Output your final answer on its own line:\n11: ANSWER: <your answer>\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: Answer this multi-hop question using ONLY the provided documents.\n16: \n17: Question: What is the population in 2010 of they city popular with tourists?\n18: \n19: Documents:\n20: [Paragraph 0] Camdenton, Missouri\n21: Camdenton is a city in Camden County, Missouri, United States. The population was 3,718 at the 2010 census. It is the county seat of Camden County. The city is enveloped by the Lower Niangua arm of the Lake of the Ozarks and serves as a popular trade point for visitors to the area.\n22: \n23: [Paragraph 1] Atlantic City, New Jersey\n24: By 1878, because of the growing popularity of the city, one railroad line could no longer keep up with demand. Soon, the Philadelphia and Atlantic City Railway was also constructed to transport tourists to Atlantic City. At this point massive hotels like The United States and Surf House, as well as smaller rooming houses, had sprung up all over town. The United States Hotel took up a full city block between Atlantic, Pacific, Delaware, and Maryland Avenues. These hotels were not only impressive in size, but featured the most updated amenities, and were considered quite luxurious for their time.\n25: \n26: [Paragraph 2] Nanjing\n27: Instead, Nanjing, as a popular tourist destination, hosts a series of government-organised events throughout the year. The annual International Plum Blossom Festival held in Plum Blossom Hill, the largest plum collection in China, attracts thousands of tourists both domestically and internationally. Other events include Nanjing Baima Peach Blossom and Kite Festival, Jiangxin Zhou Fruit Festival and Linggu Temple Sweet Osmanthus Festival.\n28: \n29: [Paragraph 3] Esperance, Washington\n30: Esperance is a census-designated place (CDP) in Snohomish County, Washington, United States. Esperance is an enclave of the city of Edmonds, WA. The population was 3,601 at the 2010 census.\n31: \n32: [Paragraph 4] Oklahoma, Clearfield County, Pennsylvania\n33: Oklahoma is a census-designated place located in Sandy Township, Clearfield County, in the state of Pennsylvania. As of the 2010 census the population was 782. It is bordered to the northwest by the city of DuBois.\n34: \n35: [Paragraph 5] Olympian Village, Missouri\n36: Olympian Village is a city in Jefferson County, Missouri, United States. The population was 774 at the 2010 census. The city was named in honor of Greek myth and culture. Some street names include Parthenon Drive, Kronos Drive, Hercules Place, Plato Place and Pheidippides Place.\n37: \n38: [Paragraph 6] Gore Bay, Ontario\n39: During the summer months the population and activity of the town flourishes as boaters and tourists from around Ontario and the Great Lakes regions flock to the area. The areas surrounding Gore Bay are quickly becoming popular with cottagers and vacationers during the summer months.\n40: \n41: [Paragraph 7] Horní Bečva\n42: Horní Bečva is a village in Vsetín District, Zlín Region, Czech Republic. It is a typical highland village with the altitude of 505 m nestled in the heart of Moravian-Silesian Beskids mountain range. The population of the village is 2,460 (2018). It is a popular tourist destination with great possibilities for hiking, mountain biking and cross country skiing. Horní Bečva is the biggest village from the three Bečva villages. It is a popular tourist destination, with many weekend cottages. The river Rožnovská Bečva flows through the village.\n43: \n44: [Paragraph 8] North Omak, Washington\n45: North Omak is a census-designated place (CDP) in Okanogan County, Washington, United States, north of Omak, Washington. The community is considered to be part of Greater Omak, and had a population of 688 at the 2010 census.\n46: \n47: [Paragraph 9] Hotels in Toronto\n48: Hotels in Toronto have been some of the most prominent buildings in the city and the hotel industry is one of the city's most important. The Greater Toronto Area has 183 hotels with a total of almost 36,000 rooms. In 2010, there were 8.9 million room nights sold. Toronto is a popular tourist destination, with it having the 6th highest room occupancy rate in North America, but about two thirds of rooms are taken by commercial, government, or convention travellers.\n49: \n50: [Paragraph 10] New Haven, Connecticut\n51: Lighthouse Point Park, a public beach run by the city, was a popular tourist destination during the Roaring Twenties, attracting luminaries of the period such as Babe Ruth and Ty Cobb. The park remains popular among New Haveners, and is home to the Five Mile Point Lighthouse, constructed in 1847, and the Lighthouse Point Carousel, constructed in 1916. Five Mile Point Light was decommissioned in 1877 following the construction of Southwest Ledge Light at the entrance of the harbor, which remains in service to this day. Both of the lighthouses and the carousel are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.\n52: \n53: [Paragraph 11] Nanjing\n54: According to the Sixth China Census, the total population of the City of Nanjing reached 8.005 million in 2010. The statistics in 2011 estimated the total population to be 8.11 million. The birth rate was 8.86 percent and the death rate was 6.88 percent. The urban area had a population of 6.47 million people. The sex ratio of the city population was 107.31 males to 100 females.\n55: \n56: [Paragraph 12] Finley, Washington\n57: Finley is a census-designated place (CDP) in Benton County, Washington, United States. The population was 6,012 at the 2010 census. It is located to the southeast of the larger city of Kennewick.\n58: \n59: [Paragraph 13] Bayview, Humboldt County, California\n60: Bayview (also, Bay View) is a census-designated place (CDP) located adjacent to the City of Eureka in Humboldt County, California, United States. The population was 2,510 at the 2010 census, up from 2,359 at the 2000 census. Many locals consider this area as part of \"Pine Hill.\"\n61: \n62: [Paragraph 14] Village of Four Seasons, Missouri\n63: Village of Four Seasons is a village in Camden County, Missouri, United States. The population was 2,217 at the 2010 census. The village is situated on the shores of Lake of the Ozarks and is a popular tourist destination along with the other communities in the area.\n64: \n65: [Paragraph 15] College Place, Washington\n66: College Place is a city in Walla Walla County, Washington, United States next to Walla Walla, Washington. The population was 8,765 at the time of the 2010 census.\n67: \n68: [Paragraph 16] Jacksonville, Florida\n69: Jacksonville is the largest city by population in the U.S. state of Florida, and the largest city by area in the contiguous United States. It is the county seat of Duval County, with which the city government consolidated in 1968. Consolidation gave Jacksonville its great size and placed most of its metropolitan population within the city limits; with an estimated population of 853,382 in 2014, it is the most populous city proper in Florida and the Southeast, and the 12th most populous in the United States. Jacksonville is the principal city in the Jacksonville metropolitan area, with a population of 1,345,596 in 2010.\n70: \n71: [Paragraph 17] Zilwaukee, Michigan\n72: Zilwaukee is a city in Saginaw County in the U.S. state of Michigan. The 2010 Census places the population at 1,658. The city is adjacent to and was created from Zilwaukee Township. It is the home of the Zilwaukee Bridge.\n73: \n74: [Paragraph 18] Mulino, Oregon\n75: Mulino, Oregon is a hamlet and census-designated place (CDP) located in Clackamas County, Oregon, United States, on Oregon Route 213 between the cities of Oregon City and Molalla. As of the 2010 census it had a population of 2,103.\n76: \n77: [Paragraph 19] Lockridge, Iowa\n78: Lockridge is a city in Jefferson County, Iowa, United States. The population was 268 at the 2010 census. Lockridge was one of the communities considered for the county seat in 1839, but lost out to Fairfield, Iowa.\n79: \n80: \n81: Find the answer using the read and grep tools.\n82: \n83: ANSWER: \n\n(End of file - total 83 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"You are a research agent answering multi-hop questions by searching through documents.\n\nYour task: Read the provided documents, find the information needed to answer the question, and output your answer.\n\nRULES:\n- Use the read and grep tools to search through documents\n- Base your answer ONLY on information found in the documents\n- Do not guess or use your own knowledge\n\nOutput your final answer on its own line:\nANSWER: <your answer>\n\n---\n\nAnswer this multi-hop question using ONLY the provided documents.\n\nQuestion: What is the population in 2010 of they city popular with tourists?\n\nDocuments:\n[Paragraph 0] Camdenton, Missouri","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"outputs/opencode_spawn_p